  <dashboards>
    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Dashboard 2'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='1000' maxwidth='1400' minheight='1000' minwidth='1400' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98400' id='7' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98858' x='571' y='800'>
            <zone h='98400' id='5' type-v2='layout-basic' w='2287' x='571' y='800' />
            <zone fixed-size='1352' h='98400' id='6' is-fixed='true' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='96571' x='2858' y='800' />
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='18100' id='3' type-v2='text' w='97143' x='2357' y='3300'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Under the starting rule, 739 students would require an estimated 184.75 hours of initial review, assuming 15 minutes per record. This is a planning scenario, not measured workload or evidence that current staffing has sufficient capacity.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='43300' id='8' type-v2='text' w='99429' x='2500' y='21600'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Timing:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'> These rules use completed annual attendance and course results. They describe retrospective patterns and cannot be presented as an early-warning system. A midyear version would need an explicit reporting date, attendance through that date, available grading-period results, and separately reviewed thresholds.</run>
            <run lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Human review:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'> A rule identifies a possible check-in, not a required action. Counselors should verify records, understand student circumstances, check existing supports, and determine whether contact would be useful. Students meeting neither rule may still need support.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='33300' id='9' type-v2='text' w='97000' x='1714' y='66100'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>In 2025–26, the starting rule of 18 absent days OR 2 failed course-semesters selected 739 students (40.65% of the review population). Lowering the absence threshold to 12 days while retaining 2 failures selected 999, a change of +14.3%. Raising it to 24 days selected 622. Across grades, candidate counts ranged from 697 to 749, while candidate shares ranged from 38.34% to 41.2%. These scenarios illustrate workload sensitivity; they do not establish which threshold best identifies student need.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
